Z||000005||Fformula88||10-22-2000||12:14 PM||||Most of todays sport compact cars use DOHC engines... and most of those are four cyls. They flash around their high HP numbers (like the '00 Celica's 180) but achieve them at high RPM's and have relatively little Torque.  The Fiero can still hold its own against these cars.  As an example, I have a 97 Probe SE (4 cyl, 118 HP) as a daily driver.  It looses in the run to 60 MPH to my Formula by about 3 seconds.  Compared to my dads Fiero coupe, I'd say its about equal in 0-60.  Being a larger and heavier car, it doesn't handle as well as either Fiero.  <P>I haven't run any V6 Eclipses yet... but with 200 HP I'd watch out for them.  However, for a 13+ year old car, the Fiero is still a good performer.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||1
